  "_note": "Cooldown values are starting estimates and are NOT verified against the current patch. Check each one in a custom game and edit here. 'starts' is 'on_use' or 'after_effect' (then 'effect' seconds are added). Optional 'callout' overrides what is said when a cooldown is back (default: '<first alias> is up'). Ults: 'cost' is ult points, checked on 2026-11-23 against the Overwatch wiki table and Blizzard's patch notes through November 2026. Where the wiki missed a patch, the cost is the wiki value times the patch % rounded to 25 (Genji, Venture, Emre, Hazard, Winston: Aug 11; Domina: Sep 8; Hanzo: June). D.Mon's cost isn't listed anywhere (0 = show time since used only). 'charge_factor' (how fast the hero charges vs the median hero) and 'hold' (seconds a full ult is typically held) come from Overwatch League 2018-19 stats; reworked or newer heroes use the role average (supports 1.2, others 0.95). 'tier' is engage, kill, save or minor and decides which ults get 'may be up' callouts and what is read out first. The first alias is the word spoken back to you. Every alias was checked against vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15: it can't hear grav, suzu, kitsune, deadeye, overclock or panopticon, which is why Zarya is 'gravity', Suzu is 'bell', Kitsune is 'fox' and Sojourn is 'sojourn'. If you add an alias, the app warns at startup when the model doesn't know it. Every alias was also run through the recognizer as synthetic speech (tools/check_speech.py): 'valk' was heard as 'bell' every time, and 'tectonic', 'hog' and 'e m p' were unreliable, hence 'valkyrie', 'quake', 'roadhog' and 'blackout'; 'spree' was heard as 'three' and 'terra' as other words, hence 'slaughter' (Shion) and 'surge' (Orisa).",
